\paragraph{Text encoder sensitivity.}
Our text probes use all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (384 dimensions), a relatively compact sentence encoder. The large dimensionality gap between HS features (4096-d) and text features (384-d) may artificially inflate the observed modality advantage on R1-8B. A stronger text encoder (e.g., E5-large at 1024 dimensions or instructor-xl at 768 dimensions) could narrow the modality gap by capturing more nuanced semantic content from reasoning steps. The relative ranking of modalities may therefore be partially contingent on text encoder capacity.

\paragraph{Limited architectural diversity.}
Two of the three tested models (DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B and QwQ-32B) share the Qwen-2.5 architecture. The sole Llama-based model (DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B) is also the only one exhibiting a clear HS probing advantage. This confound makes it difficult to disentangle whether the observed differences arise from architecture, model scale, or distillation procedure. Evaluation on a wider range of base architectures (e.g., Mistral, Gemma, LLaMA-3) is needed to resolve this ambiguity.

